---
// Why the measurement rig came first. Left: the old loopback setup — server, load
// generator, and its result-draining reader all on one box, sharing cores over the
// loopback interface, so the rig competes with the thing it measures (this is what
// capped the first post at a fake ~21k). Right: server alone on one box, two dedicated
// load boxes over a real NIC, so nothing that generates or drains load touches the
// engine's cores.
const W = 680, H = 250;
const boxW = 150, boxH = 92, colGap = 40;
// left panel
const lx = 24, ly = 96;
// right panel
const rx = 372, ry = 60;
---
<figure class="chart rigtop">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Two rigs. Left, the old loopback rig: one box holds the server, the load generator, and its reader all sharing cores over the loopback interface, so the measurement competes with the server and caps out at a false 21k. Right, the isolated rig: the server has a box to itself and two separate load-generator boxes drive it over a real network, so nothing that generates or drains load shares a core with the engine.">
    <text x={lx} y={28} class="ptitle">loopback rig — measures itself</text>
    <text x={lx} y={44} class="psub">everything shares one box's cores</text>
    <rect x={lx} y={ly} width={boxW + 130} height={boxH} rx="8" fill="var(--bg-soft)" stroke="var(--warning)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 3" />
    <text x={lx + (boxW + 130) / 2} y={ly + boxH + 16} text-anchor="middle" class="hostlbl warn">one box · loopback</text>
    {[
      { t: 'server', s: 'engine' },
      { t: 'load gen', s: 'sends orders' },
      { t: 'reader', s: 'drains replies' },
    ].map((b, i) => (
      <g>
        <rect x={lx + 12 + i * 90} y={ly + 20} width={78} height={52} rx="5" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--border)" />
        <text x={lx + 12 + i * 90 + 39} y={ly + 42} text-anchor="middle" class="btitle">{b.t}</text>
        <text x={lx + 12 + i * 90 + 39} y={ly + 58} text-anchor="middle" class="bsub">{b.s}</text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x={lx + (boxW + 130) / 2} y={ly - 8} text-anchor="middle" class="verdict warn">false ~21k ceiling</text>

    {/* divider */}
    <line x1={352} y1={20} x2={352} y2={H - 12} stroke="var(--border)" stroke-dasharray="2 4" opacity="0.6" />

    <text x={rx} y={28} class="ptitle">isolated rig — measures the server</text>
    <text x={rx} y={44} class="psub">server alone; load on its own boxes</text>
    {/* server box */}
    <rect x={rx + 90} y={ry + 14} width={120} height={54} rx="6" fill="var(--bg-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" />
    <text x={rx + 150} y={ry + 36} text-anchor="middle" class="btitle">server</text>
    <text x={rx + 150} y={ry + 52} text-anchor="middle" class="bsub">engine · 8 cores</text>
    {/* two load boxes */}
    {[0, 1].map((i) => {
      const bxy = ry + 108 + i * 4;
      const bx = rx + (i === 0 ? 6 : 168);
      return (
        <g>
          <rect x={bx} y={ry + 100} width={112} height={48} rx="6" fill="var(--bg)" stroke="var(--border)" />
          <text x={bx + 56} y={ry + 120} text-anchor="middle" class="btitle">load box {i + 1}</text>
          <text x={bx + 56} y={ry + 136} text-anchor="middle" class="bsub">125 clients</text>
          <line x1={bx + 56} y1={ry + 100} x2={rx + 150} y2={ry + 70} stroke="var(--muted)" stroke-width="1.5" />
        </g>
      );
    })}
    <text x={rx + 150} y={ry + 168} text-anchor="middle" class="verdict acc">real ~30k knee, then a hunt</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>The rig was the first decision, not an afterthought. On the left, the load generator and its reader share the server's cores over loopback, so the measurement throttles with the thing it's measuring — that's the false 21k ceiling the first post chased. On the right, the server gets a box to itself and two separate boxes drive load over a real network. Isolating it immediately showed a single load box could push the server to 49k, so 21k was never the server.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .rigtop :global(.ptitle) { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--fg); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; }
  .rigtop :global(.psub) { font-size: 11px; fill: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .rigtop :global(.btitle) { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--fg); font-family: var(--font-sans); font-weight: 600; }
  .rigtop :global(.bsub) { font-size: 10px; fill: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-sans); }
  .rigtop :global(.hostlbl) { font-size: 10px; fill: var(--muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .rigtop :global(.hostlbl.warn) { fill: var(--warning); }
  .rigtop :global(.verdict) { font-size: 11px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 600; }
  .rigtop :global(.verdict.warn) { fill: var(--warning); }
  .rigtop :global(.verdict.acc) { fill: var(--accent); }
</style>
